# The "cleanup" rule's Equipment/Fortification half (GameAction.java:1511,
# cleanupDanglingAttachments): unlike an Aura, which the same rule sends to
# its owner's graveyard, an Equipment or Fortification whose host just left
# the battlefield only becomes unattached -- it stays right where it was.
# Grizzly Bears (2/2) is a 4/4 while Sword of Body and Mind's own
# Mode$ Continuous | AddPower$ 2 | AddToughness$ 2 applies (applyContinuousPT,
# continuous.go), so 4 marked damage -- not 2 -- is what makes it lethal.
# The first state-based-action check (StartTurn's own Untap-step
# beginPhase) destroys it (CR 704.5g/h, destroyDamagedCreatures) and, the
# same pass, cleanupDanglingAttachments finds Sword of Body and Mind with
# no host left.
startturn human
